Package: birtRcpp
Type: Package
Title: BIvariate Response Time Modeling with 'Rcpp'
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Jie-Wen", "Tsai", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "tsai.jiewen@gmail.com")
Description: Item response and response time models fitted from their full conditionals.
    A built-in model is chosen with ecm(data, model = ...) or gibbs(data, model = ...): the
    two-parameter logistic model, alone or with log-normal response times (van der Linden,
    2007, <doi:10.1007/s11336-006-1478-z>), latent regressions of ability and speed,
    cross-relations between ability and the log response times, and their quantile
    (asymmetric Laplace) versions. The main estimator is ECM (ecm(); Meng and Rubin, 1993,
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/80.2.267>): one conditional maximization per block of parameters,
    Polya-Gamma bounds for logistic likelihoods (Polson, Scott and Windle, 2013,
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2013.829001>), adaptive or Bock-Aitkin quadrature (Bock and Aitkin,
    1981, <doi:10.1007/BF02293801>) with normal-linear latent variables integrated exactly, and
    Louis' standard errors. The same steps drive Gibbs sampling (gibbs(); conjugate updates and
    Metropolis-adjusted Langevin steps), with samplers in C++ ('RcppArmadillo') that port the
    'Julia' package 'ExtendedRtIrtModeling.jl' (its function names are kept as aliases). Both
    estimators have a check: check_ecm(), and check_sampler() with the Geweke (2004,
    <doi:10.1198/016214504000001132>) test and simulation-based calibration. equations() and
    algorithm() write out the model and every step, before or after fitting.
